      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable": "guacd is not reachable",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.lead": "AppEndO cannot open remote desktops until Apache Guacamole guacd is running on the machine that hosts this AppEndO process. Probed endpoint: {endpoint}. The Windows PC you want to remote into does not need guacd \u2014 only Remote Desktop (port 3389) enabled.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.commandDebian": "sudo apt update\nsudo apt install -y guacd\nsudo systemctl enable --now guacd\nsudo systemctl status guacd --no-pager",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.commandDocker": "docker run -d --name guacd --restart unless-stopped -p 4822:4822 guacamole/guacd",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.commandDockerStart": "docker start guacd",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.commandVerify": "ss -lnt | grep 4822\n# or: nc -zv 127.0.0.1 4822",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.debian": "Option B \u2014 Ubuntu / Debian package (no Docker):",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.docker": "Option A \u2014 Docker (any distro). Create the container once; later boots keep it running because of --restart unless-stopped:",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.dockerStart": "If the container already exists:",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.env": "If the probed endpoint is not 127.0.0.1:4822, set GUACD_HOST and GUACD_PORT in the AppEndO .env to match, then restart AppEndO.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.intro": "Follow this section when AppEndO is installed on Linux. Install guacd on this AppEndO host only.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.other": "Fedora, RHEL, SUSE, and other distros: prefer Docker. If a distro package exists it is usually named guacd or guacamole-server \u2014 enable and start that service, then verify port 4822 as above.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.title": "Linux host",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.linux.verify": "Confirm guacd is listening on the probed port:",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.refresh": "After guacd is listening, refresh this page. The warning clears when AppEndO can reach the endpoint.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.commandRun": "docker run -d --name guacd --restart unless-stopped -p 4822:4822 guacamole/guacd",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.commandStart": "docker start guacd",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.commandVerify": "docker ps --filter name=guacd\nTest-NetConnection 127.0.0.1 -Port 4822",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.commandWsl": "sudo apt update\nsudo apt install -y guacd\nsudo service guacd start",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.env": "If the probed endpoint is not 127.0.0.1:4822, set GUACD_HOST and GUACD_PORT in the AppEndO .env to the address Docker or WSL is actually listening on, then restart AppEndO.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.intro": "Follow this section when AppEndO is installed on Windows. Apache does not ship a native Windows guacd installer \u2014 run guacd in Docker on this AppEndO host.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.step1": "1. Install Docker Desktop for Windows and start it. Enable the WSL 2 backend during setup, then wait until Docker reports it is running.",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.step2": "2. Open PowerShell and create the container once. This publishes guacd on TCP 4822 on this machine:",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.step3": "3. If that container already exists, start it instead of creating it again:",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.step4": "4. Confirm the container is up and that port 4822 accepts connections:",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.title": "Windows host",
      "rdpHub.guacdUnreachable.windows.wsl": "If you cannot use Docker Desktop, install guacd inside WSL (Ubuntu) on this same PC and keep the service running so Windows can reach 127.0.0.1:4822:",
      "rdpHub.keepSecret": "Leave blank to keep the stored secret.",
