        slug: "identity-and-access",
        title: "Identity, roles, and sessions",
        summary: "Users, roles, JWT sessions in HttpOnly cookies, login lockout, OAuth/OIDC, and Individual/Company profiles.",
        body: md(
          "Open **Users** (`/us/studio/users`) and **Roles** (`/us/studio/roles`). The annotated screenshots mark the same Studio chrome: nav (1), title (2), workspace grid (3).",
          "## Users",
          "Create and update accounts and credentials. Dev installs use a simple username/password. Production should keep that form, then add providers \u2014 not replace it with a second login invention.",
          "## Roles and RBAC",
          "Roles are permission groups. Studio pages declare `allowRoles` in the nav registry. Unlisted users never see gated Development and Operations items. The public Home portal does not require a session.",
          "## Sessions",
          "JWTs live in **HttpOnly cookies** only \u2014 never `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`. Login lockout is part of the identity service. Google, GitHub, Microsoft Entra, and generic OIDC ship as system extensions; enterprise SAML is on the roadmap.",
          "## Profiles",
          "Individual and Company profiles attach to the same identity records. They are not a second user table."
        ),
        publishedAt: "2026-08-18T09:00:00.000Z",
