        title: "Data Studio and the Data API",
        summary: "Model edge tables visually, publish REST Data APIs with a Sequelize runtime, and introspect connected schemas.",
        body: md(
          "Open **Data Studio** (`/us/studio/data-studio`). Callout 1 is still Studio nav. The workspace (3) is the modeler \u2014 objects, fields, and publish \u2014 not a SQL scratch pad pretending to be a product.",
          "## What you build",
          "Each Edge model becomes a managed resource. Publishing exposes a REST Data API the rest of the platform (grids, forms, Server Functions, packages) can call. Introspection reads connected schemas instead of forcing you to retype every column.",
          "## Control plane versus edge",
          "`base_*` tables stay on the **control plane**. External/business data goes through **EdgeDbRouter** and registered data sources. Do not mix those paths.",
          "## Record Policy",
          "Row-level **Capability versus Scope** (organization and geography) applies on Data APIs. See the Record Policy guide \u2014 it is not the same as a Studio role."
        ),
        publishedAt: "2026-08-18T10:00:00.000Z",
