        title: "Data sources and engines",
        summary: "PostgreSQL is the verified production control plane. Extra edge sources include Postgres, SQL Server, MySQL, Oracle, MongoDB, Redis, and SQLite.",
        body: md(
          "Open **Data Sources** (`/us/studio/data-sources`). The workspace lists connections: the default control-plane database plus any extra engines you register.",
          "## Control plane",
          "Greenfield production path is **PostgreSQL**. MySQL, SQLite, and SQL Server adapters exist; wizard E2E for MySQL/SQLite is still being hardened. `npm run setup` provisions local PostgreSQL.",
          "## Edge sources",
          "Register extra databases for LOB data. Queries from Data Studio models and Server Functions must go through **EdgeDbRouter** \u2014 never ad-hoc connection strings in package UI.",
          "## Cache",
          "Hot keys and Redis live under **Cache Control**, not inside a data source row. See the Operations guide."
        ),
