        summary: "Author, simulate, publish, and run durable workflows with human work items, webhooks, timers, parallel branches, and subflows.",
        body: md(
          "Open **Workflows** (`/us/studio/workflows`). The workspace is the definition list and designer entry \u2014 not a drawing that disappears when you refresh.",
          "## Authoring",
          "Definitions are first-class records: validate, publish, import, and export. The engine is native to AppEndO, not a bolted-on BPM vendor.",
          "## Runtime",
          "Runs are durable. Waits, timers, webhooks, parallel paths, and subflows are part of the core action pack. Human **work items** land in an inbox for people who may never open the designer.",
          "## How it connects",
          "Workflows call Server Functions and Data APIs. They do not replace them. Scheduled Tasks can wake functions on cron; Jobs show long-running progress for work the engine or functions enqueue."
        ),
